From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: bound GLINK packets and quarantine ambiguous sessions

Decode exact ABI sizes before reading the little-endian return code. Preserve firmware errors, serialize pending responses, reject late replies after timeout, and drain work before teardown. No new Uke Type-C profile is enabled. A protocol timeout or service loss needs a new boot session until a wire resynchronization contract is documented.

Release 27 correction: the Uke runtime sends owner 32779/opcode 0x13,
type 2, length 24. The previous global type-1 check drops completion events
and SET_NOTIFICATION_ENABLE times out. Dispatch type validation per opcode;
retain strict reply type, owner, size, receiver and lifecycle boundaries.
Source: MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd
File: drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_glink.c (opcode-dispatched notifications)
Runtime: Fedora Rawhide, POCO Pad X1, kernel 7.2.10-26, 18 October 2026.

